{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2931","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2931","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2931\",\"parent_revision\":\"be2460dabd683ba9342a71a61fb55824f9536437\",\"root_revision\":\"1b860f0376469220a87475712a741edc33caa44917b86256461093e7bbb2389c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-17\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`_GitHubContentCache.list_content` calls `FileCache.cache_content()` once per returned record, and each call re-parses and re-serialises the entire cache state file with an `fsync`, making a single content listing O(n\u00b2) in the number of cached records \u2014 101 records cost 79s of pure local disk/serialization work with zero network involvement in a controlled measurement \u2014 so any production `list_content()` against a repo with a large content set degrades quadratically.\\n\\nWhere: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_content_migration.py:260-261` (the per-record loop) calling into `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/file_cache.py:49-75` (`cache_content`) and `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/file_cache_state.py:97-142` (`_CacheStateStore.transaction`/`_save`, which does a full YAML load+validate+dump+fsync on every single call).\\n\\nDiscovered as a side finding while investigating why the pytest suite takes 9+ minutes to run \u2014 the slow test itself is otherwise pure in-memory mock code with no real network or subprocess cost; the 79-185s it takes is entirely this write-amplification pattern.\\n\\nImpact: every code path that stores more than a handful of content records through `cache_content()` in a loop pays quadratic local disk cost, independent of GitHub API latency. Only the pytest run made this visible; the underlying defect is production code, not test infrastructure.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **filecache.cache_content() called in a loop makes github content listing o(n\u00b2) \u2014 full state file re-parsed and re-serialized per record** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 surfaced during a pytest timing investigation\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-17\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4cd1595015e7dc549e7da64aeaad794b27eb099338e6d44366287c4323b121e9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgwZ_Q\"}"}